SURVIVOR rows-over-the-limit: the tool passes `cap` (its own bound, never above the limit), so the library's constant is a second line of defence for a caller that passes more; reaching it needs more than 2^25 rows in an argument vector, which no control here builds
SURVIVOR ids-over-the-rows: with more ids than rows some id has no row, and the check for an id with no row refuses with the same code and reason; the early check only avoids allocating the work arrays for a log that is going to be refused (the allocation is bounded by the limits of the line above)
